# NOTHING MOUNTS THIS DIRECTORY ANY MORE (`PROD-01-TLS-ACME-01`, `R-146a`). The certificate pair the proxy
# serves is the one the ACME client exports into the `certs` named volume
# (`infra/acme/compose.acme.yml`); a pair placed here by hand is read by nobody.
#
# THE DIRECTORY AND ITS IGNORE RULE STAY, as a net and not as a mechanism: a key that somebody drops here out
# of habit (the old runbook told the owner to) still cannot be committed. The two lines below ignore every
# file in it except this one, so `git status` cannot tempt anybody and `git add -A` cannot take a key by
# accident. `tests/integration/composition/test_proxy_tls_path.py` asks `git check-ignore` about the names
# rather than trusting this comment.
*
!.gitignore
